  "_agreement": [
    "Telugu predicate adjectives agree with the subject's gender",
    "(పెద్దవాడు / పెద్దది), and the names here are both masculine and",
    "feminine. Every comparison is therefore phrased on the ATTRIBUTE",
    "noun rather than on the person -- 'రవి వయస్సు సీత వయస్సు కంటే",
    "ఎక్కువ', Ravi's age is more than Sita's age -- where ఎక్కువ / తక్కువ",
    "do not inflect. One template set then serves every name without a",
    "gender lexicon that could be wrong."
  ],

  "_oblique": [
    "A plural noun takes its oblique form before a postposition:",
    "మార్కులు -> మార్కుల కంటే. `than` holds the form used before కంటే,",
    "so templates never build it by string surgery."
  ],

  "_digits": [
    "ASCII digits, for both languages. Both tokenizers split them into",
    "one piece per digit, whereas Assamese digits merge into multi-digit",
    "pieces (২৫ is one piece). Using the same digits keeps numeric",
    "comparison equally hard for Model H and Model L, so a difference",
    "between them is not an artefact of number tokenization."
  ],

